A||N||7||Haze_Performance||Can a Car Dealer Ever tell the truth?||||1||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-18-2000||03:10 PM||||I passed by a dealer yesterday and saw a red 86 SE. I stoped and looked at it. They wanted $3500 for it. 4-speed, Power Windows, NO locks, sunroof, 90,000miles, all in all good shape.Well the dealer saw me pull up in my freshly washed Fiero, and said "WOW That's a real clean Fiero". After about a 1/2 hour of this guy talking about Fiero like he created them, I told him I would fair trade him for it (Just to see if me would do it) All of a sudden the Fiero went from the best car made to the hardest car to sell in the world. He changed his tune FAST "Well we are just tring to sell this one. The owner dosnt want another one on the lot".I told him to have someone look at my car and see what it was worth. He said $4500. So i asked why cant we trade?? Your getting over a $1000 deal?? So he goes back in the store for about 5min. When he returned he said that there was a kid who put down $1000 last night and he was tring to get a loan for the rest. He then said that the kid has a 86 SE and he wanted to buy this one as a parts car. (WOW a $3500 parts car, How bad could the car your driving be!!! lol).   Also you can tell the car was sitting a long time. The engine was covered in dust, tires were dry rotted and the paint had that "Dealer Just buffed the hell out of it golw" You know the glow that lasts about 3 days after you buy it. (Hey Orief!! I guess for some people need a $3500 parts car (Orange) hehe.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">    My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A><P><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 07-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||07-18-2000||03:15 PM||||He needed the 5 minutes to come up with a good cover story.  Should've taken a bit longer.  What a lying piece of crap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-18-2000||05:02 PM||||Sounds like that car salesman is a real smart bastard. You’d have to be to come up with lines like that and expect someone to buy them. Next time just look at that guy, stick you tongue out the side of your mouth and say, HUH!||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||07-18-2000||05:25 PM||||Almost every car salesman I've met is absolute filth.  I've only met a couple honest ones.  Money-grubbing pigs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||07-18-2000||06:36 PM||||Haze, wish they'da traded you! I'd a rushed right in and scooped yours up!! Even with the $1000 I already put down, your's would make a better parts car - I guess I'll wait til you make the deal...........<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/MY_SIGNATURE.gif">               <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||07-19-2000||03:08 AM||||After he said they were hard to sell and the owner wanted it off his lot you should have said you'll give him $1500 for it. The person that traded it in probably only got $500 for trade from the money grubbing #%*&%#$@$%$@#&^&^%^#(^$$##%^% !!! <BR>You should stop back over on Saturday and see if it is still there. If it is talk to a different salesman and see if you can get the car for less. Obviously nobody is going to spend $3500 for a "parts" car! Next thing he'd tell you is it's a kid who own's an orange one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ur2biteme||07-19-2000||09:19 AM||||i got swindled on mine.  i knew it was wrecked by the body damage, but i didn't know that the driver rear brake caliper was leaking (covered up), tires looked good, untill i saw the inside edges, completely bald, when it was wrecked (passenger rear corner) from the looks of things, the battery exploded which caused a lot of the problems i'm having now, the clutch master cyl was leaking, no thermostat (i wondered why i didn't have a heater).  the list goes on.  <P>the reason why i went with this one was #1  the engine sounded like it was very strong ('87 iorn duke) but needed a tune up, which i was right.  #2  the only interior flaws was SLIGHT warping of the normal dash stuff and a couple of small cigarette burns in the seats, that probably could be fixed, but i'm lazy.  #3  My mom had the money to loan me at the time beacuse i didn't have a car and i needed one.  kinda one of those, do it now or not at all things.  <P>bought it at 117k.  compression check at 137k, high cyl=151, low=142.  165k right now, still pulls harder than all the other dukes i've seen.  <P>back to the salesman thing though, yeah.  i wish i had $3500 to spend on a "parts car"||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||07-19-2000||02:17 PM||||You want a salesman to tell you the truth????<P>Ask him if he will say anything to get your money...<P>Some poor fool will probably drop the $4500 on that car.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon - Titusville, FL<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"Matched Perfect and Staggered Special"||||reg||1
